{"name":"Caramel Latte","hex":"#8c6342","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"caramel","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A smooth, chewy, sticky confection made by heating sugar and other ingredients until the sugars polymerize and become sticky.","A (sometimes hardened) piece of this confection."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a yellow-brown color."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/caramel"},{"term":"latte","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A drink of coffee made from espresso and steamed milk, generally topped with foam.","A similar drink, where the espresso is replaced with some other flavoring ingredient such as chai, maté or matcha (green tea)."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A pillar capped by a hemispherical stone capital with the flat side facing up, used as building supports by the ancient Chamorro people and now used as a sign of Chamorro identity."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/latte"}],"entries":[{"title":"Caramel","blocks":[{"text":"Caramel is a range of food ingredients made by heating sugars to high temperatures. It is used as a flavoring in puddings and desserts, as a filling in bonbons or candy bars, as a topping for ice cream and custard, and as a colorant commonly used in drinks."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Caramel-2.jpg/330px-Caramel-2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caramel"},{"title":"Latte","blocks":[{"text":"Latte or caffè latte, also known as caffellatte, caffelatte, or rarely caffè e latte, is a coffee drink of Italian origin made with espresso coffee and steamed milk, traditionally served in a glass."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Caffe_Latte_at_Pulse_Cafe.jpg/330px-Caffe_Latte_at_Pulse_Cafe.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Latte"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Caramels.jpg/500px-Caramels.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Caramels.jpg/1280px-Caramels.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Caramels.jpg/500px-Caramels.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Milk caramel manufactured as square candies, either for eating or for melting down","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACaramels.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Omar-kaare_ja_klontti_web.jpg/500px-Omar-kaare_ja_klontti_web.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Omar-kaare_ja_klontti_web.jpg/1280px-Omar-kaare_ja_klontti_web.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Omar-kaare_ja_klontti_web.jpg/500px-Omar-kaare_ja_klontti_web.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Omar caramel candies","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOmar-kaare_ja_klontti_web.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Coffee_with_milk_%28563800%29.jpg/500px-Coffee_with_milk_%28563800%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Coffee_with_milk_%28563800%29.jpg/1280px-Coffee_with_milk_%28563800%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Coffee_with_milk_%28563800%29.jpg/500px-Coffee_with_milk_%28563800%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser